    <h1>WHEN THE TROUBLE STARTED</h1>
  </header>

  <div class="story-body">

    <p>
      An (unknown at the time) administrative decision was made: normal conversation
      was clearly insufficient. A connection like this required its own, extremely
      personal language.
    </p>

    <p>
      Since we're both very much into doing things, naturally we started building one.
    </p>

    <p>
      It started with DHAT.
    </p>

    <p>
      Then DHHAT.
    </p>

    <p>
      Project Management Henda had things to say. Even a made-up language needs
      proper governance.
    </p>

    <p>
      And ultimately there was a fusing of two eggs and the DHHMT was an embryo.
    </p>

    <p>
      Obviously, it needed a cover, the only sensible colour was
      <strong>Excel green</strong>.
    </p>

    <p>
      You were less convinced.
    </p>

    <p>
      You wanted sage.
    </p>

    <p>
      Or olive.
    </p>

    <p>
      <em>Maar nie oorryp nie.</em>
    </p>

    <p>
      And a little bit of blue.
    </p>

    <p>
      Absolutely no Bollywood gold.
    </p>

    <p>
      This was, I think, our first disagreement, a colour-based constitutional crisis.
    </p>

    <p>
      The conversation could go from footwork to balls to avoidance to imaginary
      qualifications to who was going to school whom, and somehow it all made perfect
      sense.
    </p>

    <p>
      There was an email address that absolutely did not need to exist.
    </p>

    <p>
      There was talk of turning the whole thing into an ebook.
    </p>

    <p>
      And then, naturally, Philip entered the conversation.
    </p>

    <p>
      Poor Philip.
    </p>

    <p>
      Somewhere in the middle of the Dodgeball discussion, his apparent desire to join
      the lesbian community became a matter of serious consideration.
    </p>

    <p>
      We were supportive.
    </p>

    <p>
      Obviously.
    </p>

    <p>
      His career options were explored.
    </p>

    <p>
      Crackwhore.
    </p>

    <p>
      Prostitution.
    </p>

    <p>
      Lesbian.
    </p>

