    <p>
      There was also <em>Ladies First</em>, which I immediately decided you needed to
      watch because it was ridiculously inappropriate and had enough creative marketing
      nonsense in it to make me think of you.
    </p>

    <p>
      Naturally.
    </p>

    <p>
      And somewhere amongst all this nonsense, you said something that stuck with me:
      that it felt oddly familiar talking to me.
    </p>

    <p>
      It did.
    </p>

    <p>
      That was the weird part.
    </p>

    <p>
      We could be talking and then, without warning, one of us would say something real.
    </p>

    <p>
      No big transition.
    </p>

    <p>
      No warning.
    </p>

    <p>
      Just...
    </p>

    <p>
      <em>oh.</em>
    </p>

    <p>
      Even vulnerability had to sneak in sideways through the swinging door.
    </p>

    <p>
      Voicenotes with very specific instructions.
    </p>

